-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 22 (ENFORCEMENT OF JUDGMENTS AND ORDERS), rules 1 to 5: definitions, the enforcement order, satisfaction by
-- consent, discharge of a non-party, money in Court.  Rules 6 to 13 (how the Sheriff carries the order out, sale,
-- objections, examination, instalments, stay) are in roc5-o22-sheriff.l4.  LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: as in roc5-o20.l4.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are the text's own yes and no;
-- NOTHING is "not covered"; a caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Seam S-L2: nothing in Order 22 asks whether the Government is a party (Order 59 rule 11 switches Order 22 off
-- for the Government and lives in another part); the functions here keep saying what their own rule says.
-- "Subject to any written law" is not threaded as an input (NOTES.md).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 22 -- Enforcement of judgments and orders`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- definitions of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 22 r 1 component of the amount due` IS ONE OF
    `o 22 r 1 interest`
    `o 22 r 1 costs`
    `o 22 r 1 another component`

-- "includes": the two named are in; the list is not closed.
-- src:3382 | 1. In this Order, unless the context otherwise requires — “amount due to the enforcement applicant” includes interest and costs;
@ref O 22 r 1 term amount due to the enforcement applicant (src:3382-3382)
GIVEN component IS A `o 22 r 1 component of the amount due`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 1 the component is within the amount due to the enforcement applicant` MEANS
    CONSIDER component
    WHEN `o 22 r 1 interest` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 22 r 1 costs` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 22 r 1 another component` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“amount due to the enforcement applicant” includes interest and costs"

DECLARE `o 22 r 1 kind of Court order` IS ONE OF
    `o 22 r 1 a judgment or order for the payment of money (including costs)`
    `o 22 r 1 a judgment or order for the delivery of movable property`
    `o 22 r 1 a judgment or order for the title to or possession of immovable property`
    `o 22 r 1 a judgment or order for the doing of an act`
    `o 22 r 1 a judgment or order for the restraint or cessation of an act`
    `o 22 r 1 a judgment or order for the declaration of rights`
    `o 22 r 1 another kind of judgment or order`

-- src:3383 | “Court order” includes any judgment or order for the payment of money (including costs), the delivery of movable property, the title to or possession of immovable property, the doing of or the restraint or cessation of any act or the declaration of any rights;
@ref O 22 r 1 term Court order (src:3383-3383)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 22 r 1 kind of Court order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 1 the judgment or order is a Court order` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `o 22 r 1 another kind of judgment or order` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“Court order” includes any judgment or order for the payment of money (including costs), the delivery of movable property, the title to or possession of immovable property, the doing of or the restraint or cessation of any act or the declaration of any rights"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "means": closed.
-- src:3384 | “enforcement applicant” means a party or any other person who applies for or has obtained an enforcement order because the party or person is entitled to enforce any Court order;
@ref O 22 r 1 term enforcement applicant (src:3384-3384)
GIVEN `the person applies for or has obtained an enforcement order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to enforce a Court order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 1 the person is an enforcement applicant` MEANS
    IF `the person applies for or has obtained an enforcement order` AND `the person is entitled to enforce a Court order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“enforcement applicant” means a party or any other person who applies for or has obtained an enforcement order because the party or person is entitled to enforce any Court order"

DECLARE `o 22 r 1 kind of enforcement cost` IS ONE OF
    `o 22 r 1 charges, commissions, expenses and fees incurred by or payable to the Sheriff in carrying out an enforcement order`
    `o 22 r 1 costs allowed under these Rules payable to the enforcement applicant in applying for and carrying out an enforcement order`
    `o 22 r 1 expenses incurred by the enforcement applicant in applying for and carrying out an enforcement order`
    `o 22 r 1 another cost`

-- src:3385 | “enforcement costs” means the charges, commissions, expenses and fees incurred by or payable to the Sheriff in carrying out an enforcement order and the costs allowed under these Rules payable to, and all expenses incurred by, the enforcement applicant in applying for and carrying out an enforcement order;
@ref O 22 r 1 term enforcement costs (src:3385-3385)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 22 r 1 kind of enforcement cost`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 1 the cost is within the enforcement costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `o 22 r 1 another cost` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“enforcement costs” means the charges, commissions, expenses and fees incurred by or payable to the Sheriff in carrying out an enforcement order and the costs allowed under these Rules payable to, and all expenses incurred by, the enforcement applicant in applying for and carrying out an enforcement order"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3386 | “enforcement order” means an enforcement order mentioned in Rule 2;
@ref O 22 r 1 term enforcement order (src:3386-3386)
GIVEN `it is an enforcement order mentioned in Rule 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 1 the order is an enforcement order` MEANS
    IF `it is an enforcement order mentioned in Rule 2`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“enforcement order” means an enforcement order mentioned in Rule 2"

-- src:3387 | “enforcement respondent” means a party against whom an enforcement order is sought or made;
@ref O 22 r 1 term enforcement respondent (src:3387-3387)
GIVEN `the person is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
