`o 22 r 1 the person is a non-party` MEANS
    IF `an enforcement order for attachment of a debt is issued against the person` AND `it is issued to attach a debt due from that person to the enforcement respondent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“non‑party” means a person against whom an enforcement order for attachment of a debt is issued to attach a debt due from that person to the enforcement respondent"

DECLARE `o 22 r 1 kind of property` IS ONE OF
    `o 22 r 1 immovable property`
    `o 22 r 1 movable property`
    `o 22 r 1 another kind of property`

-- src:3390 | “property” or “properties” means immovable property or movable property, of whatever description.
@ref O 22 r 1 term property (src:3390-3390)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 22 r 1 kind of property`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 1 the thing is property` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `o 22 r 1 another kind of property` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“property” or “properties” means immovable property or movable property, of whatever description"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

