§§ `Rule 2 -- the enforcement order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): the enforcement applicant may apply, "without affecting any other methods of enforcement".
-- src:3392 | 2. —(1) An enforcement applicant may apply for an enforcement order to enforce one or more Court orders, without affecting any other methods of enforcement that are available to the enforcement applicant under any written law. (2) Subject to any written law, an enforcement order authorises the Sheriff to do one or more of the following: ( a )
@ref O 22 r 2(1) (src:3392-3392)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to enforce one or more Court orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 2(1) the person may apply for an enforcement order to enforce the Court orders` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to enforce one or more Court orders`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An enforcement applicant may apply for an enforcement order to enforce one or more Court orders"

-- src:3392 | 2. —(1) An enforcement applicant may apply for an enforcement order to enforce one or more Court orders, without affecting any other methods of enforcement that are available to the enforcement applicant under any written law. (2) Subject to any written law, an enforcement order authorises the Sheriff to do one or more of the following: ( a )
@ref O 22 r 2(1) (src:3392-3392)
GIVEN `another method of enforcement is available to the enforcement applicant under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 2(1) applying for an enforcement order affects the other method of enforcement` MEANS
    IF `another method of enforcement is available to the enforcement applicant under a written law`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without affecting any other methods of enforcement that are available to the enforcement applicant under any written law"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other methods of enforcement that are available to the enforcement applicant under any written law"

DECLARE `o 22 r 2(2) kind of enforcement order` IS ONE OF
    `o 22 r 2(2)(a) an enforcement order for seizure and sale of property`
    `o 22 r 2(2)(b) an enforcement order for delivery or possession of property`
    `o 22 r 2(2)(c) an enforcement order for attachment of a debt`
    `o 22 r 2(2) another enforcement order`

DECLARE `o 22 r 2(2) what the Sheriff is authorised to do` IS ONE OF
    `o 22 r 2(2)(a) seize and sell all property belonging to the enforcement respondent`
    `o 22 r 2(2)(b) seize and deliver or give possession of property in the possession or control of the enforcement respondent`
    `o 22 r 2(2)(c) attach a debt which is due to the enforcement respondent from a non-party`
    `o 22 r 2(2)(d) do anything specified in the Court order`
    `o 22 r 2(2) anything else`

-- (2): "authorises the Sheriff to do one or more of the following".  Paragraphs (a) to (c) are each "in respect of"
-- one kind of order; (d) is not tied to a kind.
-- src:3392 | 2. —(1) An enforcement applicant may apply for an enforcement order to enforce one or more Court orders, without affecting any other methods of enforcement that are available to the enforcement applicant under any written law. (2) Subject to any written law, an enforcement order authorises the Sheriff to do one or more of the following: ( a )
-- src:3393 | in respect of an enforcement order for seizure and sale of property, to seize and sell all property belonging to the enforcement respondent;
-- src:3394 | ( b )
-- src:3395 | in respect of an enforcement order for delivery or possession of property, to seize and deliver or give possession of property in the possession or control of the enforcement respondent;
-- src:3396 | ( c )
-- src:3397 | in respect of an enforcement order for attachment of a debt, to attach a debt which is due to the enforcement respondent from any non‑party, whether immediately or at some future date or at certain intervals in the future, including where the debt which is due to the enforcement respondent is represented by a deposit of money by the enforcement respondent in a non‑party that is a financial institution, whether or not the deposit has matured and despite any restriction as to the mode of withdrawal;
-- src:3398 | ( d )
-- src:3399 | to do anything specified in the Court order.
@ref O 22 r 2(2) (src:3392-3399)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 22 r 2(2) kind of enforcement order`
      thing IS A `o 22 r 2(2) what the Sheriff is authorised to do`
      `the Court order specifies the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 2(2) the enforcement order authorises the Sheriff to do the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(2)(a) seize and sell all property belonging to the enforcement respondent` THEN
        IF kind EQUALS `o 22 r 2(2)(a) an enforcement order for seizure and sale of property`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of an enforcement order for seizure and sale of property"
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(2)(b) seize and deliver or give possession of property in the possession or control of the enforcement respondent` THEN
        IF kind EQUALS `o 22 r 2(2)(b) an enforcement order for delivery or possession of property`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of an enforcement order for delivery or possession of property"
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(2)(c) attach a debt which is due to the enforcement respondent from a non-party` THEN
        IF kind EQUALS `o 22 r 2(2)(c) an enforcement order for attachment of a debt`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of an enforcement order for attachment of a debt"
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(2)(d) do anything specified in the Court order` THEN
        IF `the Court order specifies the thing`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to do anything specified in the Court order"
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(2) anything else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph lists four things and does not say the Sheriff may not do others

-- (2)(c): the debt may be due now, later or at intervals, and a deposit with a financial institution counts
-- "whether or not the deposit has matured and despite any restriction as to the mode of withdrawal".
-- src:3396 | ( c )
-- src:3397 | in respect of an enforcement order for attachment of a debt, to attach a debt which is due to the enforcement respondent from any non‑party, whether immediately or at some future date or at certain intervals in the future, including where the debt which is due to the enforcement respondent is represented by a deposit of money by the enforcement respondent in a non‑party that is a financial institution, whether or not the deposit has matured and despite any restriction as to the mode of withdrawal;
@ref O 22 r 2(2)(c) (src:3396-3397)
GIVEN `the debt is due to the enforcement respondent from a non-party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 2(2)(c) the debt may be attached` MEANS
    IF `the debt is due to the enforcement respondent from a non-party`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the text adds "whether immediately or at some future date or at certain intervals in the future", so the time at which the debt falls due does not matter
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a debt which is due to the enforcement respondent from any non‑party"

-- src:3396 | ( c )
-- src:3397 | in respect of an enforcement order for attachment of a debt, to attach a debt which is due to the enforcement respondent from any non‑party, whether immediately or at some future date or at certain intervals in the future, including where the debt which is due to the enforcement respondent is represented by a deposit of money by the enforcement respondent in a non‑party that is a financial institution, whether or not the deposit has matured and despite any restriction as to the mode of withdrawal;
@ref O 22 r 2(2)(c) (src:3396-3397)
GIVEN `the deposit of money was made by the enforcement respondent in a non-party that is a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 2(2)(c) the deposit may be attached whether or not it has matured and despite any restriction as to the mode of withdrawal` MEANS
    IF `the deposit of money was made by the enforcement respondent in a non-party that is a financial institution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "including where the debt which is due to the enforcement respondent is represented by a deposit of money by the enforcement respondent in a non‑party that is a financial institution"

