@ref O 22 r 2(4) (src:3401-3432)
GIVEN item IS A `o 22 r 2(4) item`
      `more than 6 years have passed since the date of the Court order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a change has occurred in the identity of the enforcement applicant or the enforcement respondent since the date of the Court order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court order requires the enforcement respondent to pay money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `interest is payable and continues to accumulate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a specific property is to be seized, other than property already specified in the Court order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the specific property is not in the possession or control of the enforcement respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a deposit of money or other debt due to the enforcement respondent from any non-party is to be attached` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 2(4) the affidavit must state the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(4)(a) the terms of the Court order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(4)(b) the enforcement respondent's name and address` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(4)(c) the date that the Court order was served on the enforcement respondent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(4)(d) the terms of the Court order which have not been complied with and which are to be enforced` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(4)(e) the reasons for the delay in the application` THEN
        IF `more than 6 years have passed since the date of the Court order`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where more than 6 years have passed since the date of the Court order" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(4)(f) the change in the identity of the enforcement applicant or the enforcement respondent` THEN
        IF `a change has occurred in the identity of the enforcement applicant or the enforcement respondent since the date of the Court order`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where any change has occurred in the identity of the enforcement applicant or the enforcement respondent since the date of the Court order" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(4)(g) the amount due, the amount recovered from any security, the amount paid and the amount that remains owing` THEN
        IF `the Court order requires the enforcement respondent to pay money`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Court order requires the enforcement respondent to pay money"
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(4)(h) the amount of interest owing daily from the time of making the affidavit` THEN
        IF `interest is payable and continues to accumulate`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if interest is payable and continues to accumulate"
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(4)(i) the description of the specific property and the evidence that it belongs to or is in the possession or control of the enforcement respondent` THEN
        IF `a specific property is to be seized, other than property already specified in the Court order`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a specific property is to be seized, other than property already specified in the Court order"
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(4)(j) the evidence that all persons in actual possession or control of the specific property have been notified about the application` THEN
        IF `the specific property is not in the possession or control of the enforcement respondent`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the specific property is not in the possession or control of the enforcement respondent"
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(4)(k) the description of the deposit of money or debt and the evidence that it belongs or is due to the enforcement respondent` THEN
        IF `a deposit of money or other debt due to the enforcement respondent from any non-party is to be attached`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a deposit of money or other debt due to the enforcement respondent from any non‑party is to be attached"
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(4)(l) whether the Sheriff is to enforce the parts of the enforcement order in a particular sequence or simultaneously` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 22 r 2(4)(m) the undertaking` THEN JUST TRUE

-- (4)(m): the undertaking is given by the applicant's solicitors if the applicant has solicitors, and by the
-- applicant if not, on three matters, and a written undertaking stating them is exhibited.
