-- src:3427 | indemnify the Sheriff against all claims, costs and expenses arising from complying with the enforcement order;
-- src:3428 | (ii)
-- src:3429 | pay upon request all charges, commissions, expenses and fees incurred by or payable to the Sheriff in complying with the enforcement order; and
-- src:3430 | (iii)
-- src:3431 | deposit the amount of money requested by the Sheriff before the Sheriff complies with the enforcement order and from time to time,
-- src:3432 | and exhibit a written undertaking stating the matters in sub‑paragraph ( m )(i), (ii) and (iii).
@ref O 22 r 2(4)(m) (src:3425-3432)
GIVEN `the enforcement applicant is represented by solicitors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is given by the solicitors for the enforcement applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is given by the enforcement applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it undertakes to indemnify the Sheriff against all claims, costs and expenses arising from complying with the enforcement order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it undertakes to pay upon request all charges, commissions, expenses and fees incurred by or payable to the Sheriff in complying with the enforcement order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it undertakes to deposit the amount of money requested by the Sheriff before the Sheriff complies with the enforcement order and from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written undertaking stating those matters is exhibited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 2(4)(m) the affidavit states the undertaking and exhibits it as the rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the enforcement applicant is represented by solicitors` AND (NOT `the undertaking is given by the solicitors for the enforcement applicant`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that the solicitors for the enforcement applicant (if the enforcement applicant is represented by solicitors) or the enforcement applicant (if the enforcement applicant is not represented by solicitors) undertake to"
        IF (NOT `the enforcement applicant is represented by solicitors`) AND (NOT `the undertaking is given by the enforcement applicant`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or the enforcement applicant (if the enforcement applicant is not represented by solicitors) undertake to"
        IF `it undertakes to indemnify the Sheriff against all claims, costs and expenses arising from complying with the enforcement order`
           AND `it undertakes to pay upon request all charges, commissions, expenses and fees incurred by or payable to the Sheriff in complying with the enforcement order`
           AND `it undertakes to deposit the amount of money requested by the Sheriff before the Sheriff complies with the enforcement order and from time to time`
           AND `a written undertaking stating those matters is exhibited`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and exhibit a written undertaking stating the matters in sub‑paragraph ( m )(i), (ii) and (iii)"

`o 22 r 2(5) the period of validity of an enforcement order in the first instance` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 12
    `period unit` IS Months
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- (5): valid "in the first instance for 12 months beginning with the date of issue" (subject to (8)); the last day of
-- the 12 months is the O 3 r 3 count from the date of issue.
-- src:3433 | (5) Subject to paragraph (8), an enforcement order is valid in the first instance for 12 months beginning with the date of issue.
@ref O 22 r 2(5) (src:3433-3433)
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the date of issue` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the enforcement applicant has given written notice to the Sheriff not to take further action on the enforcement order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has ordered under Rule 3 that satisfaction be recorded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 2(5) the enforcement order is valid in the first instance on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `o 22 r 2(8) the enforcement order has ceased to be valid` `the enforcement applicant has given written notice to the Sheriff not to take further action on the enforcement order` `the Court has ordered under Rule 3 that satisfaction be recorded` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (8)" [paragraph (8): "An enforcement order ceases to be valid"]
        IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the date of issue`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "valid in the first instance for 12 months beginning with the date of issue" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]
        IF `the day asked about` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "valid in the first instance for 12 months beginning with the date of issue" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]

`o 22 r 2(6) the period of each extension` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 12
    `period unit` IS Months
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- (6): the Court "may by order extend the validity ... for a period of 12 months", where the costs and the amount
-- due have not been fully satisfied or the respondent has not complied with all the terms of the Court order, "if
-- an application for extension is made to the Court before the day on which the enforcement order would otherwise
-- expire".
-- src:3434 | (6) Where the enforcement costs and the amount due to the enforcement applicant have not been fully satisfied or the enforcement respondent has not complied with all the terms of the Court order, the Court may by order extend the validity of the enforcement order from time to time for a period of 12 months at any time beginning with the day on which the order is made, if an application for extension is made to the Court before the day on which the enforcement order would otherwise expire.
@ref O 22 r 2(6) (src:3434-3434)
GIVEN `the enforcement costs and the amount due to the enforcement applicant have not been fully satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enforcement respondent has not complied with all the terms of the Court order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the application for extension is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the enforcement order would otherwise expire` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 2(6) the Court may extend the validity of the enforcement order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the enforcement costs and the amount due to the enforcement applicant have not been fully satisfied` OR `the enforcement respondent has not complied with all the terms of the Court order`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the enforcement costs and the amount due to the enforcement applicant have not been fully satisfied or the enforcement respondent has not complied with all the terms of the Court order" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
        IF `the date the application for extension is made` LESS THAN `the day on which the enforcement order would otherwise expire`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if an application for extension is made to the Court before the day on which the enforcement order would otherwise expire" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]

-- (7): priority runs from the original issue, "the validity of which has been extended under paragraph (6)".
-- src:3435 | (7) The priority of an enforcement order, the validity of which has been extended under paragraph (6), is to be determined by reference to the date on which it was originally issued.
@ref O 22 r 2(7) (src:3435-3435)
GIVEN `the validity of the enforcement order has been extended under paragraph (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the enforcement order was originally issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 22 r 2(7) the date by reference to which the priority is determined` MEANS
    IF `the validity of the enforcement order has been extended under paragraph (6)`
    THEN JUST `the date the enforcement order was originally issued`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The priority of an enforcement order, the validity of which has been extended under paragraph (6)"

-- src:3435 | (7) The priority of an enforcement order, the validity of which has been extended under paragraph (6), is to be determined by reference to the date on which it was originally issued.
@ref O 22 r 2(7) (src:3435-3435)
GIVEN `the validity of the enforcement order has been extended under paragraph (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 2(7) the priority is determined by reference to the date of original issue` MEANS
    IF `the validity of the enforcement order has been extended under paragraph (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The priority of an enforcement order, the validity of which has been extended under paragraph (6)"

-- (8): the two events after which an enforcement order ceases to be valid.
-- src:3436 | (8) An enforcement order ceases to be valid — ( a )
-- src:3437 | after the enforcement applicant gives written notice to the Sheriff not to take further action on the enforcement order because the enforcement respondent has complied with all the terms of the Court order or for any other reason; or
-- src:3438 | ( b )
-- src:3439 | after an order of the Court for satisfaction to be recorded is made under Rule 3.
@ref O 22 r 2(8) (src:3436-3439)
GIVEN `the enforcement applicant has given written notice to the Sheriff not to take further action on the enforcement order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has ordered under Rule 3 that satisfaction be recorded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 2(8) the enforcement order has ceased to be valid` MEANS
    IF `the enforcement applicant has given written notice to the Sheriff not to take further action on the enforcement order` OR `the Court has ordered under Rule 3 that satisfaction be recorded`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "An enforcement order ceases to be valid — ( a ) after ... or ( b ) after ..." and the paragraph does not say these are the only ways validity ends (paragraph (5) ends it by lapse of time)

